# JUDO

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physiological, biomechanical, technical and tactical demands of Judo.

Its purpose is to enable the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to understand the unique performance profile of judoka and to individualize physical preparation accordingly.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Judo is a grappling combat sport focused on throwing, controlling and submitting an opponent through the efficient application of balance, leverage and timing.

Success depends upon:

Kuzushi (Off-Balancing).

Tsukuri (Positioning).

Kake (Execution).

Control.

Grip Fighting.

Timing.

Technical Precision.

---

# Philosophy

Judo is the efficient application of force.

The objective is not to overpower the opponent.

The objective is to destabilize the opponent while remaining mechanically efficient.

Maximum efficiency with minimum necessary effort remains a fundamental principle of Judo.

